.#-----------------------------------------------------
.input|xwiki/2.1
.# Test that the block content located in table cells that can't be rendered as Markdown inside a table row is
.# rendered on a single line: standalone macros are rendered as inline macros (the line endings of their content
.# being rendered as line breaks), HTML is rendered as inline HTML (its line endings being replaced by spaces) and
.# tables are rendered as inline HTML tables (keeping the Markdown syntax of their cell contents), unless they contain
.# wiki syntax (e.g. macros) which isn't parsed inside inline HTML, in which case their rows are rendered as text
.#-----------------------------------------------------
|=a|=b
|x|(((
{{info}}
hello
{{/info}}
)))
|y|(((
para

{{mymacro param="value"}}
line1
line2
{{/mymacro}}
)))
|z|(((
{{html}}
<p>
html
</p>
{{/html}}

after
)))
|w|(((
before

(% class="nested" hidden %)
|=(% rowspan="2" %)n1|n2
|(% colspan="2" %)n3 ~| **n4**

after
)))
|v|(((
|{{info}}m{{/info}}|[[Space.Page]]
|n3|n4
)))
.#-----------------------------------------------------
.expect|markdown/1.2
.#-----------------------------------------------------
|  a  | b |
| --- | --- |
|  x  | {{info}}hello{{/info}} |
|  y  | para<br/><br/>{{mymacro param="value"}}line1<br/>line2{{/mymacro}} |
|  z  | <p> html </p><br/><br/>after |
|  w  | before<br/><br/><table class="nested" hidden=""><tr><th rowspan="2">n1</th><td>n2</td></tr><tr><td colspan="2">n3 \| **n4**</td></tr></table><br/><br/>after |
|  v  | {{info}}m{{/info}} \| [[Space.Page]]<br/>n3 \| n4 |
